{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/pulls/413","id":3847563109,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSbOoU87lVSdl","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/413","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/413.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/413.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/413","number":413,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(numeric_list): recover coding context for bare follow-ups (#412)","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nFixes #412 — a bare numeric-list follow-up answered `unknown`.\n\nThe deployed assistant held a Russian coding conversation. The first turn\nestablished a full coding context (JavaScript, \"give me the code and the\nresult\"). The bare follow-up — **`Отсортируй 4, 3, 1, 17, 8, 9, 15`** — names no\nlanguage and does not ask for code, so the **stateless** numeric-list handler\ndeclined it and the request fell through every specialized handler to `unknown`.\n\nA human reads that follow-up as \"do the same thing to this new list.\" The solver\nnow does too: it recovers the language (and the code request) from the\nconversation and continues the coding context — idiomatic code in the\nestablished language plus the deterministically-computed result.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`src/solver_handlers/numeric_list/mod.rs` (and its `src/web/formal_ai_worker.js`\nmirror) inspected only the current prompt. Its language gate\n`program_language_by_alias(normalized)?` returns `None` for the bare follow-up,\nso the handler bailed before computing anything. Nothing consulted the\nconversation, so an established coding context could not carry over.\n\n## The fix\n\n- **`numeric_list_history_context(history)`** scans the conversation newest-first\n  and inherits the language / code request **only** from a prior turn that was\n  itself a genuine numeric-list coding request (recognised operation + supported\n  language + ≥2 numbers). Unrelated chatter (e.g. \"What is the capital of\n  France?\") therefore never leaks a language.\n- The current prompt's own language always wins; a reduction (`sum`, …) follow-up\n  inherits the code request. A `numeric_list_coreference` trace event records\n  what was inherited.\n- `src/solver.rs` threads the conversation `history` into\n  `handle_specialized_pattern` so the `numeric_list` handler runs the\n  history-aware entry point.\n- **Full-codebase parity:** the same logic is mirrored byte-for-byte in the\n  browser worker (`tryNumericList(prompt, history)`), and the 170-cell\n  cross-runtime parity matrix stays byte-identical.\n\nThe change is purely additive for every existing (history-free) case.\n\n## How to reproduce\n\n```\ncargo run --example repro_issue_412\n```\n\nprints `intent = write_program`, the JavaScript code for the new list, and\n`Результат: 1, 3, 4, 8, 9, 15, 17`, with a trace showing the inherited language\nand the meta-language CST engine (`cst_engine meta_language`).\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/integration/issue_412_followup_sort.rs` — 4 tests: the reported\n  follow-up recovers JavaScript + code + sorted result; a no-context bare prompt\n  stays non-`write_program` (no fabricated language); a reduction follow-up\n  inherits the code request; an English/Python context inherits across a bare\n  English follow-up.\n- `experiments/issue-412-js-numeric-list-coreference.mjs` — the same scenarios\n  through the JS worker in a node-VM sandbox (incl. an unrelated-context\n  negative): all pass.\n- `experiments/issue-395-cross-runtime-codegen-parity.mjs` — 170/170 cells\n  byte-identical (no regression).\n- `tests/integration/issue_412_oracle_languages.rs` + the\n  `source_tests/{knowledge,solver_handler_oracle}` suites — the coding oracle\n  (R6) and the bounded-cache ratchet (R8).\n- `experiments/issue-412-js-oracle.mjs` — the worker's oracle path, byte-identical\n  to the Rust `solve()` output.\n- Full suites green under `-Dwarnings`: `cargo test --test source` (387),\n  `--test unit` (814), `--test integration` (35), `cargo clippy --all-targets`;\n  total-closure audit 0 unresolved.\n\n## Repository-wide mandate (R6–R8)\n\nIssue #412 also demanded broad, repository-wide generalization, delivered **in\nthis PR** (not deferred):\n\n- **R6 — external knowledge bases as cached APIs.** `src/knowledge.rs` models\n  Rosetta Code / Wikifunctions / Hello World Collection / Stack Overflow as\n  external sources treated as APIs even though they expose none. The\n  `write_program` fallback (`src/solver_handler_oracle.rs`, mirrored in the\n  worker) answers languages the verified catalogue never templated\n  (Kotlin/Swift/PHP/Bash/Lua/Haskell hello-world + a Rosetta-Code Kotlin\n  factorial) from an embedded popular-case cache — snippet + deterministic\n  output + source attribution — while catalogued languages keep their verified\n  route. A gated live-refresh (the existing `FORMAL_AI_LIVE_API` discipline) is\n  what would materialise per-source `data/cache/<slug>/` buckets.\n- **R8 — bounded cache.** `cache_capacity` / `within_cache_capacity` /\n  `KNOWLEDGE_CACHE_FLOOR` enforce `min(1%, 512)` clamped to source size, with a\n  ratchet test that fails CI if the committed snapshot set exceeds the cap.\n- **R7 — meta-algorithm that builds algorithms.** The compositional foundation\n  ships (the numeric-list path builds programs by composing scaffolds + idioms\n  from `data/seed/coding-idioms.lino`, validated through the meta-language CST —\n  \"add an operation/language = add seed data, not code\"). Unifying the remaining\n  bespoke coding handlers under one task-agnostic composer is a larger\n  first-principles refactor; its status and the scoping question are tracked in\n  [`docs/case-studies/issue-412/README.md`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-412-1f5f93827186/docs/case-studies/issue-412/README.md)\n  §7.4 and the PR thread.\n\nSee the deep case study under\n[`docs/case-studies/issue-412/`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-412-1f5f93827186/docs/case-studies/issue-412/README.md)\nfor the full requirement-by-requirement breakdown (R1–R12) and online research.\n","created_at":"2026-06-11T13:27:46Z","updated_at":"2026-06-11T16:54:12Z","closed_at":"2026-06-11T16:54:12Z","merged_at":"2026-06-11T16:54:12Z","merge_commit_sha":"6903828d44f0d9922e38cdb78bc5fbcc1f78733d","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k